  "excerpt": "Built on a Mercedes Sprinter 170 AWD chassis, the Obsidian Overlander was designed to take on remote terrain without sacrificing comfort. Outfitted with an 800Ah lithium battery bank, 400W solar system, and a 3000W pure ",
  "body": [
    "Built on a Mercedes Sprinter 170 AWD chassis, the Obsidian Overlander was designed to take on remote terrain without sacrificing comfort. Outfitted with an 800Ah lithium battery bank, 400W solar system, and a 3000W pure sine inverter, this van is engineered for long-term off-grid living. Shore power and DC-DC charging provide backup when needed, and the electrical system supports a full suite of outlets, devices and appliances, including a microwave, refrigerator with freezer, and an in-counter induction cooktop.",
    "Inside, the van reflects a refined yet rugged aesthetic. White cabinetry contrasts with a smoke gray wood ceiling and Havana-stained butcher block countertops. The fully tiled indoor shower and Zuvo water filtration system bring spa-level amenities to life on the road, supported by a 33-gallon fresh water tank and grey water system. A Laveo dry flush toilet offers easy waste management with zero hassle, while both indoor and outdoor showers extend usability in any climate.",
    "Performance upgrades set the Obsidian Overlander apart. Outfitted with an Agile Off Road RIP lift kit, all-terrain tires, and a Lost Saguaro rear tire carrier, this van is ready for any overlanding route. Exterior LED lighting, roof rack with side ladder, and a high-performance Starlink kit provide visibility and connectivity from anywhere. Even practical details like the electric awning, extended range fuel tank, and upgraded perimeter lighting were chosen with exploration in mind.",
    "Passenger comfort includes a queen memory foam bed, swivel-mounted TV setup, foldaway seat with CRS hooks, and magnetic blackout shades for all windows. With climate control from a diesel heater, rooftop A/C, and Maxxair fan, the Obsidian Overlander is equipped to handle all four seasons. Whether parked in a pine forest or perched on red rock, this custom-built 4 4 Sprinter offers the ultimate in mobile freedom and design-forward functionality."
  ],
